  "summary": "Four supplied documents directly apply multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling—the requested Bayesian hierarchical-model formulation—to predicting protein molecular function. Fischer et al. report F1=0.87 on MetroFlow [V0164]; El-Sayed et al. report AUROC=0.80 on ChurnBench [V0163]; Duarte et al. report MAE=0.73 on FireScope [V0162]; and Chen et al. report accuracy=0.66 on ProtMap [V0161]. Because the datasets and metrics differ, these numerical results are not directly comparable; the four direct matches are ordered by recency. No fifth supplied candidate satisfies both the method and topic requirements. [V0147] is therefore listed fifth only to meet the required five-ID format: it addresses protein molecular function on ChurnBench but uses message passing over relational graphs, reporting AUROC=0.71, so it is a comparator rather than evidence for the requested Bayesian hierarchical method.",
